A||||8||ChopTop||Misaligned Steering wheel||||1||
Z||000000||ChopTop||10-04-2001||07:56 AM||||A couple years ago I had some suspension work done on my vehicle.  After I picked it up I noticed the steerwheel was misaligned approximately one to two inches.  Anyone know how to fix this?  Thanks in advance.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||10-04-2001||08:21 AM||||They didn't do the alignment correctly. They need to do the alignment with the steering wheel centered. When everything was replaced, the front wheels were centered then adjusted. What I mean is if the suspension had the passenger side put on and you had a 10* toe out, the front end was centered so on the machine the wheels showed 5* toe out on each side. Then it was aligned. The steering wheel needs to be centered then the front needs to be re-aligned. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||10-04-2001||08:26 AM||||Other thing I have done is take out the steering wheel and reinstall it more centered. Still may not get it totally centered. The best is the alignment.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChopTop||10-04-2001||12:39 PM||||Actually I had urethane bushing installed in the front, the misaligned steering wheel was the the result of that.  I was hoping to buy new tires and wheels before I had an alignment performed, I still might wait considering it sits in the garage most of the time, or try the removing and reinstalling the steering wheel suggestion.  Thanks guys.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||10-04-2001||01:55 PM||||I believe the steering wheel only goes on one way. To get by until you get an alignment you can center the wheel by adjusting each outer tie rod end by EXACTLY the same amount. Be careful, think twice about which way it needs to go, make sure you adjust one shorter by exactly the same amount as the other gets longer. Try one turn to begin with. Test drive it and readjust if neccessary.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Back On Holiday||10-04-2001||02:12 PM||||if the Allignment is correct, put the wheels straight as possible and pull the steering wheel and slip her back on straight.<BR><P>------------------<BR>84se Silver 2m4<BR>86se Silver 2m6||||reg||1
Z||000006||LZeitgeist||10-04-2001||02:22 PM||||You can only move the steering wheel about one or two splines on the shaft before you begin running into problems with the horn button wiring connector running into problems with the hardware inside the steering wheel.<P>It's better to have the shop re-do the alignment like they should have done the first time, or if too much time has passed to go back and ask them to correct their error, make sure the shop you choose does it correctly the next time you get an alignment. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Butter||10-04-2001||02:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>They didn't do the alignment correctly. They need to do the alignment with the steering wheel centered. When everything was replaced, the front wheels were centered then adjusted. What I mean is if the suspension had the passenger side put on and you had a 10* toe out, the front end was centered so on the machine the wheels showed 5* toe out on each side. Then it was aligned. The steering wheel needs to be centered then the front needs to be re-aligned. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree with Oreif.  There is a dot on the shaft the steering wheel fits on.  This dot is offset to one side and should point toward the top of the steering wheel.  You can see this if you remove the horn button.  If this is in the correct position then when the steering wheel is straight and tires are basically pointed forward then the rack is centered and there should be the same amount of steering to the left as the right.  This should be centered upon alignment.  If it is not then the alignment was not done correctly.  This is more critical on a vehicle with a steering box as the steering ratio is not linear like a rack.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex4mula||10-04-2001||02:49 PM||||I have removed and centered mine at least twice in the last 10 years. But I have a Grant wheel. Still don't know why it can't be done with the stock one but I don't remember how a stock one looks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
